{{name}} dev
A work loop for the reviews and pull requests that reach you.

[bold]USAGE[/]
  [cyan]{{command}}[/] [dim]<command>[/] [arguments]

[bold]GET STARTED[/]
  [cyan]init[/]                   Set up from zero: config, agent homes, the app
  [cyan]doctor[/]                 Diagnose the setup without changing anything

[bold]PULL REQUESTS[/]
  [cyan]act[/]                    Resolve a unit's open items, replies as drafts
  [cyan]address[/]                Triage the reviews and failing checks of yours
  [cyan]nudge[/]                  Ask whoever it waits on for the next step
  [cyan]review[/]                 Review someone else's pull request in its own worktree
  [cyan]start[/]                  Start new work from a brief
  [cyan]take-over[/]              Make a pull request someone else opened yours
  [cyan]remove[/]                 Delete the workspace of a merged or closed one

[bold]WHAT WAITS ON YOU[/]
  [cyan]status[/]                 Pull requests by view, those needing you first
  [cyan]tui[/]                    The same views in the terminal, one-key actions
  [cyan]open[/]                   The cockpit, a workspace or a pull request
  [cyan]outbox[/]                 Drafts waiting for your approval, and yours
  [cyan]explore[/]                Open pull requests of others to help on

[bold]AUTOMATION[/]
  [cyan]plan[/]                   What the workflows would do now, and why
  [cyan]pause/resume[/]           Stop or restart automatic rounds
  [cyan]track/untrack[/]          Follow a pull request out of scope, or stop
  [cyan]mute/unmute[/]            Leave or rejoin the pending views
  [cyan]workflows[/]              The facts and steps a workflow can use

[bold]PROFILE[/]
  [cyan]profile show[/]           The blocks that apply to a repository
  [cyan]profile where[/]          The block a new rule goes in
  [cyan]profile add[/]            Add a rule to the profile
  [cyan]profile check[/]          Load the profile and list its problems
  [cyan]profile try[/]            A review round that publishes nothing
  [cyan]profile schema[/]         The JSON Schemas of the profile files, for editors

[bold]SLACK[/]
  [cyan]slack login/logout[/]     Connect to Slack, or disconnect
  [cyan]slack status[/]           Who you are logged in to Slack as
  [cyan]slack send[/]             Post as you to a thread, channel or person
  [cyan]slack follow/unfollow[/]  Admit every message of a thread, or stop

[bold]SETUP[/]
  [cyan]install[/]                Write the hooks, MCP and skills into agent homes
  [cyan]app install[/]            macOS: the app, menu bar and the daemon at login
  [cyan]trust[/]                  Trust a repository in an agent home
  [cyan]uninstall[/]              Take out what install and app install set up
  [cyan]store migrate[/]          Migrate the store to this release's schema
  [cyan]store restore[/]          Put a backup of the store back
  [cyan]config get[/]             Print a configuration value
  [cyan]version[/]                Print the version

[bold]TROUBLESHOOTING[/]
  [cyan]timings[/]                Review, merge and turn durations, waits, tokens
  [cyan]intake[/]                 Follow, start or cancel an intake
  [cyan]brief refresh[/]          Make a pull request's brief again
  [cyan]turn show[/]              A pull request's turns and their records
  [cyan]probe[/]                  Prove an agent home end to end

[bold]FOR AGENTS AND SCRIPTS[/]
  [cyan]instructions[/]           Run a turn by hand from an agent session
  [cyan]turn end/answer[/]        Record how a turn ended; read your answer
  [cyan]hook[/]                   The agent hooks install writes
  [cyan]serve[/]                  Run the daemon
  [cyan]app[/]                    macOS: the menu bar and notifications

Run '{{command}} <command> --help' for its flags and examples.
Docs: [link https://{{name}}hq.github.io/{{name}}/]https://{{name}}hq.github.io/{{name}}/[/]
